---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/marketing/PageHero.astro';
import '../styles/pages.css';
---

<Layout
  title="About FairMind | Evidence infrastructure for AI assurance"
  description="FairMind is a vendor-neutral AI assurance evidence workbench built around capability truth, human review, retained failure history, and portable evidence."
>
  <div class="route-page">
    <PageHero
      signal="Why FairMind exists"
      title="AI assurance has a"
      accent="continuity problem."
      description="Tests happen in one tool, system identity in another, framework mappings in spreadsheets, remediation in tickets, and final review in a document assembled under deadline. FairMind exists to preserve that chain as evidence moves."
      proofs={[
        { label: 'Problem', value: 'Fragmented evidence', note: 'The result loses scope, thresholds, artifacts, limitations, and review history.' },
        { label: 'Product', value: 'Evidence workbench', note: 'A vendor-neutral layer between evaluators and accountable governance.' },
        { label: 'Principle', value: 'No silent promotion', note: 'Metadata stays metadata. Missing evidence stays missing. Review stays human.' },
      ]}
      primary={{ label: 'See what is novel', href: '#novelty' }}
      secondary={{ label: 'Inspect the workflow', href: '/features' }}
    />

    <section class="route-section" id="novelty" aria-labelledby="novelty-title">
      <header class="route-section-heading">
        <h2 id="novelty-title">The novelty is not another score.</h2>
        <p>FairMind’s product thesis is that trustworthy governance depends on durable relationships between evidence objects, decisions, and change over time.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="route-ledger">
        <article class="route-ledger-row"><span>Portable unit</span><h3>Evidence Passport</h3><p>A target exchange contract that binds the tested subject, evaluator, threshold, artifact, limitation, review, remediation, and superseding rerun.</p></article>
        <article class="route-ledger-row"><span>Explicit boundary</span><h3>Capability truth</h3><p>Every evaluator declares validated, metadata-only, external-provider, unavailable, or insufficient-data state.</p></article>
        <article class="route-ledger-row"><span>Human control</span><h3>Reviewed mapping</h3><p>Technical evidence can suggest a framework relationship. An accountable person decides whether that relationship is accepted.</p></article>
        <article class="route-ledger-row"><span>Temporal truth</span><h3>Failure-preserving retest</h3><p>A clean rerun supersedes the failed evidence without deleting what failed, who acted, or why the new result was accepted.</p></article>
        <article class="route-ledger-row"><span>Reusable output</span><h3>Framework-pinned manifest</h3><p>The same accepted evidence can support several versioned frameworks while keeping the underlying technical claim bounded.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="route-section route-section-dark" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
      <div class="route-split">
        <div class="route-split-copy"><h2 id="principles-title">Built for skeptical reviewers.</h2><p>FairMind should make it easier to reject an overstated claim, inspect its source, find the unresolved blocker, and reproduce the package—not merely make a dashboard look complete.</p></div>
        <div class="route-checklist">
          <div><span>01</span><strong>Evidence before readiness</strong></div>
          <div><span>02</span><strong>Limitations beside results</strong></div>
          <div><span>03</span><strong>Human decisions with rationale</strong></div>
          <div><span>04</span><strong>Research claims bounded by measurement status</strong></div>
          <div><span>05</span><strong>Open interfaces before another closed evaluator</strong></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="route-closing" aria-labelledby="about-closing-title">
      <div><p>Bring your tests</p><h2 id="about-closing-title">Produce evidence you can defend.</h2></div>
      <div class="route-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/request-access">Work with FairMind</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/blog">Read the research notes</a></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
